, MASAAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A bearing (4) is set upright on a substrate (1) to hold an entire shaft (6) except both ends.  A rotor case (10) comprises a rotor base (11) arranged under an optical pickup (13) and having a magnet (9) inside, and a rotor boss (12) connected fixedly on the rotor base (11) in such a manner that its side is opposed to the side of the optical pickup (13).  In such a simple and small structure, the axis of the shaft (6) can be correctly maintained.  The manufacturing costs can be considerably reduced by using parts (1, 2, 5, 9, 11) that are compatible with other thin motors.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon l'invention, un support (4) est disposé verticalement sur un substrat (1) pour soutenir un arbre complet (6) sauf aux extrémités de ce dernier. Un boîtier du rotor (10) comprend un socle du rotor (11) disposé sous un capteur optique (13) et dont l'intérieur comporte un aimant (9). Le boîtier du rotor comprend également un bossage du rotor (12) fixé au socle du rotor (11) de sorte que son côté soit opposé au côté du capteur optique (13). Dans cette configuration simple et compacte, l'axe de l'arbre (6) peut être maintenu correctement. Les coûts de fabrication peuvent être considérablement réduits par l'utilisation de pièces (1, 2, 5, 9, 11) compatibles avec d'autres moteurs plats.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>